&P130279 = SNAT 519 
#atf: lang sux 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. 1(disz) dumu-munus da-da# nu-zah3-am3 
#tr.en: It was (the case) that the daughter of Dada did not escape. 
2. ensi2-ke4 
#tr.en: The governor 
3. i7-pa-e3 en3 in-na-an-tar 
#tr.en: (about this) Ipa’e asked. 
4. i3-zah3 in-na-an-du11 
#tr.en: “She escaped,” (Ipa’e) told him. 
5. ki-bi-ta nu-tuku4 mu-gub 
#tr.en: (But) from that place she did not move, she stayed there. 
6. ensi2-ra 
#tr.en: (With) the governor 
7. du11-ga-ni si nu-un-na-an-sa2 
#tr.en: his statement did (Ipa’e) not put in order;
# i.e., he was not straightforward with the governor 
@reverse 
1. iti sze-kar-ra-gal2-la 
#tr.en: month “Barley brought to the harbor,” 
2. mu {d}szu-{d}suen lugal uri5#[{ki}]-ma#-ke4 ma-da za#-[ab-sza]-li#{ki} mu#-[hul] 
#tr.en: year: “Šū-Suen, king of Ur, the lands of Zabšali destroyed.” 
@seal 1 
1. i7-pa-e3 
#tr.en: Ipa’e, 
2. dub-sar 
#tr.en: scribe, 
3. dumu lu2-{d}[szara2] 
#tr.en: son of Lu-Šara, 
4. sa12-du5 
#tr.en: the field registrar. 

